{"id":"000VQT","title":"Do Not Cross (Infections)","author":"gdc","solvedCount":3,"difficulty":4,"rating":"N/A","firstSeen":"2026-10-28T18:53:57+00:00","posted":"Heute, 17:31 Uhr","rules":"Epsode 5 of the Norma L. Dokes series. Thanks SnapDragon, MattYDdraig, Jake, NicoD and henrypijames (among others) for testing.\n\nRules\n\nNormal sudoku rules apply.\n\nInfection Sources: Each digit matching its box number is an \"infection source\". Each row and column contains an infection source. They are infected.\n\nTransmission: Infected cells infect all smaller orthogonal neighbors. Infections keep spreading until no infected cell has a smaller uninfected orthogonal neighbor. (Every infected cell can be traced back to one or more infection sources).\n\nBattenberg: A 2x2 forms a checkerboard pattern of infected and uninfected cells if and only if there is a striped cross on its central vertex.\n\nKropki Tablets join consecutive digits.\n\nClick on the image to play!\n\nExample Puzzle\n\nA 6x6 puzzle with the same rules and its solution. Colors: Orange for Infection sources, red for secondary infections and green for uninfected.\n\n→","solutionCode":"Uninfected cells in column 5, top to bottom (up to 8 digits).","tags":["Sudoku","Kropki Pairs (Variante)","Battenburg (Variante)","Modifier Cells (Variante)"],"links":[{"url":"https://sudokupad.app/ra8y9pdeof","kind":"sudokupad"},{"url":"https://tinyurl.com/normaldokes","kind":"short"}],"data":"","error":null,"settings":{},"link":"https://sudokupad.app/ra8y9pdeof","linkKind":"sudokupad","summary":{"format":"scl","decoded":true,"rows":9,"cols":9,"cages":0,"hasSolution":true,"features":["lines","overlays"]},"attempts":0,"fetched":"2026-10-28T18:53:57+00:00"}